  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 100 AM CDT Fri Oct 2 2026\n\nFrost/freeze potential... Frost/freeze setup on track for tonight,\ncontinuing at times through early next week as cooler air\ncontinues to filter in. Have blended in some NBM 10th percentile \nto decrease lows for tonight by a degree or two with high sitting \noverhead and decent window for clearing. NBM still showing healthy\nsignal (60 to 90+%) for lows below 33 degrees over north-central\ninto far northeast Wisconsin late tonight into Saturday morning, \nthough many of the CAMs are not as aggressive. Regardless, have \nopted to throw out a Frost Advisory due to solid signal for under \n36 degrees. Could potentially see a few counties being upgraded to\na Freeze Warning, though was hesitant to do so on this shift due\nto the potential for increasing mid clouds mitigating temperatures\nlate tonight. Next chance for a more widespread frost/freeze \nevent then comes Sunday night into Monday morning, with \ntemperatures in the mid 30s even sneaking down toward the Fox \nValley. Expect additional headlines to be issued during this time.\n\nDry pattern ahead... Rain chances over the course of the extended\nwill be sparse at best, with our next chances for light rain\narriving Saturday evening. Transient shortwave energy will\naccompany the passage of a clipper-like low over the upper Midwest\nSaturday evening and night, generating isentropically forced \nshowers for areas mainly north of Hwy 29. However, abundance of\nlow level dry air will result in a meager 20 to 40% chance for \nreceiving 0.25\" of QPF through Sunday morning. Otherwise, high\npressure will be the main driver of the synoptic pattern through \nat least the middle of next week, bringing abnormally dry weather\nfrom the Plains to the Midwest. This does not bode well for\nnorthern Wisconsin where D2 (Severe) to D4 (Exceptional) drought\nconditions exist. Next chances for more widespread rain don't arrive\nuntil Wednesday, though if this week is anything to go by, high \npressure could end up putting up a good fight.",
